WEBVTT

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
Run at once towards a dream

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
yume no mukou e ikkini hashitte yo

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.780
Let’s meet and laugh away yesterday’s troubles

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.780
nayameru kinou wo fungiri warai aou

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
When our memories were here,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
omoide ga itta no toki mo

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
even though we are deeply hurt, go straight on

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
kizu wo fukai no ni massugu mae ni

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.650
GO TO NEW WORLD

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
I can feel it in the wind

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
kaze no naka kanjiteru yo

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
The hot beat is shining

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
atsui kodou kagayaku yo

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
especially now…

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
ima koso

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
surely, always, you’ll be by my side

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
kitto zutto soba ni iru yo ne

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
Keep on running the way to the future.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
mirai no michi wo hashiri tsuzukeyou

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
more and more, no matter what happens

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
motto motto nani ga okitemo

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
half our tears become double smiles

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
namida wa hanbun nibai no egao ni naru

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
forever

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
itsudemo

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:39.160
In Shiritori, you take turns saying a word that start with the last syllable of the previous word.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:35.810
Go… Gorilla.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.950
Rappa. <i>(Trumpet)</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.160
Pa… Pan-Panda!

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.260
Once a word ending in “n” is said, the game ends.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:39.960
Daria.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.260
How fast!

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.060
Umm…

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.260
Amenbo. <i>(Water Strider)</i>

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.710
Boushi. <i>(Hat)</i>

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.050
Shimauma. <i>(Zebra)</i>

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.210
Manto. <i>(Cape)</i>

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.460
To… Tofu.

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.300
Futakoi?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.270
Does such a word even exist?

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.010
I wonder.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:01:59.810
Same blood type…

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.110
According to statistics on the blood types for people who eat bread versus those who eat rice,

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.000
the most common type for both groups is type A,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.710
but the second most common is more interesting.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.480
The second one in different, they say.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.660
What is the second one?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.860
For people who eat bread, after A-type, B-type is the most numerous.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.960
For people who eat rice, 0-type is the most numerous.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.500
Rentarou, you’re B-type?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.200
I dunno.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:25.880
Really?

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.460
What is a B-type person like?

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.210
B-type is…

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:32.710
Futakoi!

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.910
Shiritori again?

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:36.810
Futakoi-i-i…

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.920
Setting off on a good day

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:37.920
Ii hi tabitachi.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.930
You’re hitting your stride.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.930
Ch… Choushi detekita.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.410
Going out once in a while.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.410
Tama ni wa dekakeyo.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.160
All right! Where are we going?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.160
Yoshi! Doko e iku?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.940
Kunitachi.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.610
Chi… Choufu?

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.910
Florida!!

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:52.650
Daruma,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.160
Let’s watch some TV first.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.160
Ma…Mazu wa terebi demo mite.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.960
Let’s watch the weather forecast!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.960
Tenki yohuo demo mite.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:02:59.240
Noooo waaay…

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.240
From looking at this…

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.240
This time the drama…

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.830
Woooow!!!

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.260
Here’s the weather forecast for the Kanto region.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.560
It will be cloudy today,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.760
with a 10 percent chance of rain.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.360
Due to a low pressure front over the Sea of Japan,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:19.160
the temperature will drop, and it will be the coldest day of the year.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.360
Since the atmosphere will be dry, please be careful around fire.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.090
Well then everyone, goodbye.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:28.610
Hey.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.680
Um…

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.580
Should we go to Takashimaya?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:43.410
Well, I…

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.460
I… was thinking that, too.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:03.260
And just like that, Shirogane Sara left our regular triangle.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:35.460
I’m back.

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.190
It’s just me by myself now.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:46.610
What should I do?

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:50.710
What should I do?

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:54.910
Really…

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.930
I thought that it sounded
very typical of Sara.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.660
Unlike those around her,
who did things hesitantly,

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.660
she was always decisive,
and did everything on her own.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:47.050
Starting today, this will be your home.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.290
Yes.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.110
You’ll catch a cold.
You should take a shower.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:08.300
Deciding things by herself,
and doing everything alone.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:10.860
Sara-chan is…

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.060
Sara-chan is…!!!

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.160
It really sounds typical of Sara.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.660
Yes. Right now, somehow…

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.810
Yeah, I think it’s all right.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:29.560
Yes.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.360
To have caused such painful memories…

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.460
No.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.710
I’m sorry that you had to go out of your way to cell me.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:37.610
It’s only natural.

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.210
I’m also worried about Soujyo.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:44.410
Also, even now, you are
Sara’s real guardian.

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:45.210
Right?

00:06:48.260 --> 00:06:49.810
Hey, Futaba-kun.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:50.860
Yes.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:55.560
I think it might be better if this were
the last time we contacted each other.

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:58.910
For me, for Sara… and for you two as well.

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:02.860
I know that it is a shameless suggestion…

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:04.360
Understood.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.440
I also think that that’s for the best.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:23.710
Make love to us.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.010
W-wait!

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.960
That’s bothersome!

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:39.460
Please give it back!

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:41.210
What are you?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.410
Am I the only one who thinks this is weird?

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:44.760
Welcome everyone--

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.720
And just like that, Shirogane Sara left our regular triangle.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.810
That’s a miserable story, Lala-chan.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.040
That’s a miserable story, Lulu-chan.

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:01.260
How touching!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.410
And then, during those two days,

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:14.370
the two of us swung between reality and illusion like a violent pendulum,

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.220
constantly going back and forth.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:20.860
Welcome.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:33.860
Hey!

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:34.750
Yeah?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:38.260
You’re thinking we shouldn’t be upset about this, right?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:38.910
I guess so.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:42.160
You’re thinking that if we’re depressed, it’d wasted Sara-chan’s efforts, right?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:43.410
I guess so.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:46.000
So… let’s buy plenty of things!

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:46.960
Yeah.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.090
In short…

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.090
Yes?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.090
Let’s have lots and lots of fun!

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.610
That probably might be a…

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.360
Very good idea!

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:56.680
That is probably correct!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.910
Hey, Soujyu!

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.260
Do you know anything fun?

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:04.110
Yes!

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.210
Like what?

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.100
Like what, you say!

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:12.610
Like… like riding a shopping cart!

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.820
All right!

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:17.060
Or clattering noisily up the escalators!

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:17.820
All right!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.410
Or sweeping past the cashiers!

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.410
All right!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.710
Wait! Wait!

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:26.010
Having security guards hot on your heels!

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:27.420
All right!

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.710
Not… enough… strength… Recharge… in… elevator…

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:44.560
Recharge…

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:46.160
A-all right…

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:46.160
There are people here.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.010
Hey, Soujyu!

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:15.710
Yeah!

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.860
Life is wonderful!

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:21.210
The world is beautiful!

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:22.740
It’s so intense!

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:28.860
Definitely, we’re so satisfied that it’s as if we could fly through the sky!

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:31.280
Yes, even above that high sky.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.960
Ready…

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.240
GO!

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.740
LET’S GO!!!

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:39.910
These are clatter, clatter, clatter sound effect noises.

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:49.640
“If”… this is what I hypothesized.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.810
If we flew through the sky…

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.410
Would we be able to be happy?

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:07.980
If… if, back then, I had made love to Sara and Soujyu,

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.790
would we have been able to become happy?

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.210
There are no “if”s.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:42.810
There is only the assumption of “what if” and the wish that “it had turned out like that”.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.720
There is no absolute truth
which supports this.

00:11:46.710 --> 00:11:48.910
There is no preparation to accept what is there,

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:52.850
only tightfisted sentiment and bitter illusion.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:58.190
That’s something that elementary school brats know very well of.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:10.110
It’s just, even if they say they understand it,

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:14.340
they can’t possibly understand things that they haven’t done or experienced.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.610
Ah… I get the feeling that this is all useless.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.060
The harsh reality.

00:12:35.710 --> 00:12:39.480
For example, spending a month recovering after a traffic accident…

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.030
Nidaime!!!

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.530
He’s not stopping?

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:50.860
Gen-san!

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.420
Nidaime!

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:02.270
For example, having your house completely razed by a fire.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.860
It’s dangerous, so don’t try and come any closer!

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:21.260
I’ll rip ya bastards apart!

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.410
There, get back, get back!

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.410
Get back, please get back!

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:57.190
Re-Rentarou?

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:00.650
We’ll start over again, start over!

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:03.060
Start over, gosh-darnit!

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.760
We definitely can’t go on like this!

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.260
Rather than leaving it as it is…

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:09.940
We’ll just keep starting all over again!

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:15.290
Re-Rentarou!

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.120
Stop!!

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:28.180
I’m asking you, Nidaime.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:35.860
Like I said, we have confirmed the presence of gasoline….

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:39.460
We know that it wasn’t
because you smoked.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.610
You’re not trying to
hide the culprit, are you?

00:14:42.460 --> 00:14:43.760
I know nothing about it.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.910
Don’t say such things.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.960
It’s not like you’re the only one affected by this.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:51.510
That would also be cruel to
Gen-san from the first floor.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.210
Not only did his house get burnt down,

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:56.560
but Gen-san himself
needs a month to recover.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.410
Though it was really his own fault that he fell and hurt himself.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:00.010
I’m definitely not involved.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:02.610
THAT’S ENOUGH!

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.760
You’re like those brats who don’t know anything, dammit.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:07.610
Just hurry up and tell us and you can hurry up and go freakin’ home!

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:10.010
That’s already the third time for this month, the third time!

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:12.900
Bastard, I don’t know what’s happened,

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:15.890
but people in this town have been attacked without reason.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:19.460
Us investigating here and there have made us freakin’ freakin’ freakin’ freakin’ busy!

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:23.010
But still we have to deal with you, a freakin’ brat who knows nothing?!

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:27.260
If you keep not cooperating with our investigation,

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:29.160
I am just gonna have to whoop your--

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.010
I’m like that too.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.760
I’m freakin’ suffering as well.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.310
N-Nidaime.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.960
Translator’s Note: Katsudon = pork on rice.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.960
Wanna eat some Katsudon?

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.060
Yes.

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.860
Geez. Where do I put this coal?

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:00.660
We, put it over there please.

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.940
Even so, I just can’t reach Nidaime at all.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.110
Yeah.

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:35.620
There are no “if”s.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.810
We won’t be able to regain those days ever again.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:45.970
The burned-down office won’t
return to its old state anymore.

00:17:09.260 --> 00:17:10.710
All right, it’s over!

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:11.510
What?

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:13.410
Somehow, I feel relieved.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:16.010
Laughing and crying with all my might, eating carelessly,

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:18.110
it feels like I’ve just let it all out.

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:19.560
What good timing.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:23.480
When something new is started, this is the way to do it.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:27.830
More like, there’s no choice but to start over.

00:17:34.210 --> 00:17:39.410
In other words, pleased to meet you all over gain!

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:39.910
Right?

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:49.480
There are no “if”s.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:10.710
Back then, I didn’t fly through the sky.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.860
I didn’t hold on tightly to Sara and Soujyu.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.660
I wasn’t able to stop
the gas-wielding pyromaniac.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:31.010
There are no “if”s.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.560
There is only the present.

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:52.620
You can go first.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:29.910
Back then, I wasn’t able to make love to Sara and Soujyu.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:36.420
That’s why…

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:54.310
I wanted to star over.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.360
Dammit!

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:24.260
We demand to start over again.

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:39.600
We…

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.710
Even so, I…

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:54.890
If I think about it…

00:21:56.560 --> 00:22:01.790
If we were able to fly through the sky, would we have become happy?

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:10.410
If… I had made love to Sara and Soujyu that time… would we have become happy?

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:28.900
Inside my memories,

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:28.900
kioku no naka ni aru

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.040
there was a happy moment

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.040
shiawase na shunkan

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:41.010
within the light.

00:22:35.670 --> 00:22:41.010
hikari no naka de ita

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:47.650
It overflowed in this place.

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:47.650
afureteta kono basho de

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:51.050
For example, 3 years later,

00:22:48.120 --> 00:22:51.050
tatoeba sen nen go

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:55.260
would you be able

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:55.260
bokura no jikan wo

00:22:55.390 --> 00:23:01.660
to remember our time?

00:22:55.390 --> 00:23:01.660
omoida ni suru koto dekiru ka na

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:06.500
Ah... the days gone by

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:06.500
aa owatta hibi ga

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:15.010
always wrench my heart.

00:23:06.700 --> 00:23:15.010
KOKORO no zutto zutto shimetsuketeku

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:20.080
Hey, more than before,

00:23:15.310 --> 00:23:20.080
nee mae yori motto

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:27.760
understand the feelings of love.

00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:27.760
itoshiku omou kimochi wo shitte

